  "recipeCuisine": "Italy",
  "name": "Risotto with Radicchio and Sea Scallops",
  "text": "Risotto with Radicchio and Sea Scallops\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nYield: 4 to 6\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the scallops\n\n1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil,\n\n1/2 lb sea scallops (diced into 1/2\" pieces),\n\n1 garlic clove (minced),\n\n1/2 tsp salt (plus more to taste).\n\nFor the risotto\n\n6 cups vegetable broth,\n\n4 tbsp unsalted butter,\n\n1/2 small onion (minced),\n\n2 cups arborio rice,\n\n1 cup dry white wine,\n\n3 medium heads of radicchio (leaves),\n\nGround black pepper (to taste).\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Heat the oil in a medium frying pan over high heat. Fry the scallops until barely golden (2 minutes).\n\n2. Season with salt and set aside.\n\n3. Bring the broth to the boil then kept warm over a low heat.\n\n4.  Melt 3 tbsp butter in a large heavy pan over a medium heat.\n\n5. When the butter begins to foam add the onions. Cook until pale yellow and soft (4 - 5 minutes).\n\n6. Add the rice, stir to coat with the butter, and cook until it turns white (2 minutes).\n\n7. Add the wine and stir until absorbed.\n\n8. Add the radicchio and a ladle of stock and stir until the broth has been absorbed.\n\n9. Continue adding the stock a ladle at a time, stirring to absorb before adding the next.\n\n10. Add the scallops and their juices and mix well.\n\n11. Add a knob of butter. Mix and season.",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT20M",
  "recipeYield": "4 to 6",
